MerkleAdapterOracleGuard
├── when authenticated reports exceed movement limits
│   ├── it caches the exact report while accepted valuation remains usable
│   ├── it emits the full report and rejection status without indexed fields and replaces prior cached payloads
│   ├── it handles zero baselines, exact boundaries and fractional precision
│   └── it tracks accepted and rejected report state independently across report sequences
├── when capital flows around a snapshot
│   ├── it compares performance against the capital present at the snapshot
│   ├── post-snapshot inflows cannot dilute the loss limit
│   ├── post-snapshot outflows cannot shrink the comparison baseline
│   └── actual withdrawals cannot hide losses in the remaining portfolio
├── when a guard reviews a report
│   ├── it requires the exact authenticated cached payload
│   ├── it cannot bypass snapshot ordering or authentication and emits the accepted report bytes
│   └── it can accept a successful forwarder delivery without another execution
├── when roles or configuration change
│   ├── it keeps guard and limits roles independent and enumerable
│   ├── it enforces every multicall authorization atomically
│   ├── it rejects uint32 limits above 100% and noncanonical wider calldata without changing packed state
│   └── it preserves accounting and pending demand across workflow rotation
└── when an accepted report is delayed
    ├── latestSnapshot and adapter NAV remain readable after a long delay
    ├── delayed delivery can advance the accepted snapshot
    ├── vault flows and request updates remain available
    └── authorized account management remains available
